    "created_at": "2022-10-22T14:13:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-10-22T14:15:47Z",
    "body": "```\r\nstarship print-config\r\n```\r\n\r\nprints values in single quotes. For example:\r\n\r\n```\r\nformat = '$all'\r\n```\r\n\r\nIs there a reason why the configuration documentation uses double quotes? It would seem more consistent to me if the documentation would also use single quotes.\r\n\r\nIt would also match my personal preference of using single quotes because there is less necessity of escaping characters.\r\n\r\nThe only thing TOML literal strings (single quotes) do not allow because of lack of escaping is single quotes (`'`) *(while unicode characters like `‘` or `’` are still possible)*.\r\n\r\nTOML double quotes [require escaping](https://toml.io/en/v1.0.0#string) “quotation mark, backslash, and the control characters other than tab”\r\n\r\nLooking through `starship print-config`, the only escaping I see is for Starship symbols. Nothing that makes use of double quote strings over string literals.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/starship/starship/issues/comments/1287804863/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
